      "description": "Coagulated raw water first passes through the central flocculation zone, where slow paddles (velocity gradient G ≈ 20–70 s⁻¹) let tiny particles collide and grow into flocs. The water then moves outward and upward through the clarifier zone at low surface loading (≈ 1–2 m/h); flocs settle and are raked to the central sludge pit; clear water overflows the peripheral weir.",
